From 2f33faba0d63fba0d7289aebd27f02a88e1f5f91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 19:57:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 22/42] transports+configstore: per-tenant provider keys CRUD
 under /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{provider}/keys
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the most-requested ergonomic gap on the per-tenant admin
surface: operators can now rotate per-tenant credentials (add new
key, switch the rotation flag, delete the old key) without recreating
the whole provider.

configstore additions (delegate-then-verify; CreateProviderKeyForTenant
also pins tenant_id on the new TableKey row so it stays visible only to
the calling tenant):
- ConfigStore.GetProviderKeysForTenant — filters both the provider join
  AND the config_keys rows by tenant_id, so a tenant with a same-named
  provider as another tenant cannot see the other tenant's keys.
- ConfigStore.GetProviderKeyForTenant — single-row variant that collapses
  to ErrNotFound on cross-tenant probes.
- ConfigStore.CreateProviderKeyForTenant — refactored CreateProviderKey
  through createProviderKeyInternal so both the legacy (DefaultTenantID
  pinned) and the tenant-scoped form share the create logic. The new
  TableKey row gets tenant_id explicitly so it's only visible to the
  calling tenant.
- ConfigStore.DeleteProviderKeyForTenant — verify-then-delegate around
  the existing DeleteProviderKey transaction.
- MockConfigStore stubs added (single-implementation delegation).
- Tests cover: per-tenant rotation flow with two tenants holding
  same-named providers; cross-tenant create rejection (ErrNotFound);
  cross-tenant get/delete probes returning ErrNotFound.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantProviderHandler gains listProviderKeys, createProviderKey,
  getProviderKey, deleteProviderKey under
  /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{provider}/keys[/{key_id}]. POST mints a
  UUID for id when omitted; list + get redact key values on the wire so
  an operator UI cannot read back stored secrets via the admin API.
  POST + DELETE evict the per-tenant runtime so the next inference
  acquires with the new key set.
- Handler tests cover: happy-path create with evict, parent-not-found
  404, missing fields 400, list redaction, get cross-tenant 404,
  delete happy-path with evict.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
